      "sample_filtering_criteria": "The study starts from the PISA 2015 database and selects 53 countries/economies out of 72 participating because the remaining 19 had missing/void values caused by a technical error. The analytic sample consists of 79,963 15-year-olds. The dependent variable is dichotomized using PISA science proficiency levels: high performers are those at proficiency Level 6 with science scores above 633.33, and low performers are those at Levels 1a and 1b. For modeling, missing and invalid questionnaire data are discarded, then the remaining missing values are imputed using a nearest-neighbor mean approach; ordinal variables are converted to dummy variables and features are centered and variance-scaled."
    },
